course: dictionary
lesson: 7562
title: Prepositions: small words, big jobs
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A preposition is a small word that links a noun or pronoun to other words in a sentence. It often tells us where, when or how. In, on, under, behind, after, with, by, to and from are all prepositions.
explain: «The cat hid under the table.» Under is the preposition. It links the cat to the table and tells us where the cat is. Change it to «The cat hid on the table» and the meaning changes completely, so one small word can matter a lot.
explain: Prepositions can also tell us when: «after lunch», «on Monday», «in the morning». The word after a preposition is usually a noun or pronoun, like lunch, Monday or it. Together they make a prepositional phrase.
fact: A preposition is a small word that shows how a noun or pronoun is linked to other words.
fact: Prepositions often tell where, when or how, as in «under the table», «after lunch» and «with care».
fact: The noun or pronoun usually comes after the preposition, as in «on the desk» or «behind it».
fact: Position words in maths, such as above, below, between and next to, are prepositions too.
fact: «Preposition» also has a rare, formal meaning: an idea put forward. This is very rare, and «proposition» is usually used for that.
exercise: «The cat hid under the table.» Which word is the preposition? | cat | hid | *under | table
exercise: «We played football after lunch.» Which small word shows when? | football | played | *after | We
exercise: What is the preposition in «a pencil under the desk»? | a | desk | pencil | *under
test: «The hungry fox quickly ate the cake under the table.» Which word is a preposition? | *under | quickly | hungry | fox
test: «Sam sat beside his brother.» Which word is the preposition? | sat | *beside | brother | Sam
exam: «Mia put her bag behind the door.» Which word is a preposition, and what does it show? | put | Mia | *behind, showing where | door
